From 7f870f7c0b8e6f1c6876b6814f948c9b7a81bcd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alia Holes <thealiaholes@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:12:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] sms: show sent messages right away until the phone
 confirms them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A message sent from the desktop only appeared once the phone echoed it back,
and on a new-conversation page it never appeared: the echo was dropped as an
update for a thread the page did not know yet.

Add the message to the conversation at once, marked "Sending…", and replace
it with the phone's copy when that arrives. If no copy arrives within two
minutes the row says "Not confirmed by the phone yet", and if the daemon
reports messageSendFailed it says "Not sent: <reason>". A page started for a
new recipient adopts the thread of the first message to or from that
recipient, from either conversationCreated or conversationUpdated, so later
messages land on the page too.
